      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the first digit of the base 8 representation of $473_{10}$, we need to convert the decimal number to its binary representation first and then convert the binary representation to its base 8 representation.\n\nUsing base 10, the binary representation can be found as follows:\n11 > 3\n100 > 4\n110 > 6\n101 > 5\n111 > 7\n\nSo, the binary representation of 473_${10}$ is 11011101_2.\n\nNow, we need to convert 101_2 to its corresponding decimal value:\n1 x $10^1$ + 0 x $10^0$ = 101\n\nFinally, we convert the binary conversion result to its base 8 representation. A binary number has 0s and 1s, and each group of three binary digits corresponds to a three-digit octal number (which is base 8).\n\nSo, 101_2 is equal to (2^3-2) + (-2+0)_8.\n\nThus, the first digit of the base 8 representation of 473_$10$ is 2.",
